{:edb/db-before-t 1645 :edb/db-after-t 1646 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534958 50 #inst "2026-10-08T12:07:11.174Z" 13194139534958 true] [17592186064164 1020 #edb/ref 17592186322611 13194139534958 true] [17592186064165 1020 #edb/ref 17592186322615 13194139534958 true] [17592186064166 1020 #edb/ref 17592186322618 13194139534958 true] [17592186064458 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534958 true] [17592186064458 1100 "The following table gives the values of $f(x), f^{′}(x), g(x)$, and $g^{′}(x)$ at some points. Find $(f^{-1} \\cdot g)^{′}(2)$ of the product of functions.\n\n| **$x$** | $f(x)$ | $f^{′}(x)$ | $g(x)$ | $g^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $2$ | $-1$ | $-6$ | $-3$ | $1$ |\n| $-1$ | $2$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $-2$ |" 13194139534958 false] [17592186064458 1100 "The following table gives the values of $f(x),{f}^{′}(x),g(x),$ and ${g}^{′}(x)$ at some points. Find $({f}^{-1}\\cdot g)^{′}(2)$ of the product of functions.\n\n| **$x$** | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $-1$ | $-6$ | $-3$ | $1$ |\n| $-1$ | $2$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $-2$ |" 13194139534958 true] [17592186064458 1145 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse ${f}^{-1}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nUsing this, and the product rule, the derivative of the function ${f}^{-1}(x)g(x)$ is\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1}\\cdot g)^{′}(x)=\\frac{g(x)}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}+{g}^{′}(x){f}^{-1}(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=2,$ we have\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1}\\cdot g)^{′}(2)=\\frac{g(2)}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(2))}+{g}^{′}(2){f}^{-1}(2).\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we obtain ${f}^{-1}(2)=-1,$ $g(2)=-3,$ ${g}^{′}(2)=1,$ and ${f}^{′}(-1)=-2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1}\\cdot g)^{′}(2) & =\\frac{g(2)}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(2))}+{g}^{′}(2){f}^{-1}(2) \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{{f}^{′}(-1)}+1\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{-2}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322611 1017 #edb/ref 17592186322612 13194139534958 true] [17592186322611 1089 "q-312579" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322611 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534958 true] [17592186322611 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{2}+2$ and the point $P(2,6)$ that lies on $y=f(x).$ Given that $f(x)$ is invertible in the vicinity of $P,$ calculate ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(6).$\n\n${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(6)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322611 1113 #uuid "b1f6eff9-e354-50e5-b0d6-7aed9742e28f" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322611 1145 "We start by calculating the derivative of $f$ at the point $(2,6).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={x}^{2}+2 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =2x \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(2,6)$ lies on $y=f(x),$ we know that the corresponding point $(6,2)$ lies on $y={f}^{-1}(x).$\n\nFurthermore, the slopes of the tangents to the two respective points are reciprocals. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(6) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(6))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322613 13194139534958 true] [17592186322612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322614 13194139534958 true] [17592186322612 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534958 true] [17592186322612 1041 "field-1" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322612 1104 #edb/ref 17592186322613 13194139534958 true] [17592186322612 1110 #uuid "822f713b-c25e-5da8-a950-9db41fcefb5b" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322613 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322613 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534958 true] [17592186322613 1111 #uuid "5595ee00-3e08-5c85-ab82-a1dbb68af433" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322614 1034 "4" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322614 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534958 true] [17592186322614 1111 #uuid "83ac79de-d929-59e9-b4cd-f03e4d332524" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322615 1017 #edb/ref 17592186322616 13194139534958 true] [17592186322615 1089 "q-342590" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322615 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534958 true] [17592186322615 1100 "Find $({f}^{-1})^{′}(4)$ given the following table of values of functions $f(x)$ and ${f}^{′}(x)$ at some points.\n\n| **$x$** | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $0$ | $-9$ |\n| $-3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n\n$({f}^{-1})^{′}(4)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322615 1113 #uuid "7df6d9e2-babf-58ce-9866-244bf8f9f09d" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322615 1145 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse is\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=4,$ we have\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(4)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(4))}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we obtain ${f}^{-1}(4)=-3$ and ${f}^{′}(-3)=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{′}(4) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(4))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322616 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322617 13194139534958 true] [17592186322616 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534958 true] [17592186322616 1041 "field-1" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322616 1104 #edb/ref 17592186322617 13194139534958 true] [17592186322616 1110 #uuid "0bd4a4ca-ec2e-5073-8084-214da8c0af9e" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322617 1034 "\\frac{1}{5}" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322617 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534958 true] [17592186322617 1111 #uuid "8903ae29-e0ca-5771-860f-2c4ceea3982d" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322618 1017 #edb/ref 17592186322619 13194139534958 true] [17592186322618 1089 "q-342604" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322618 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534958 true] [17592186322618 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)=\\frac{x}{x-2}.$ Given that $y=f(x)$ is invertible throughout its domain, determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(-1).$\n\n$({f}^{-1})^{′}(-1)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322618 1113 #uuid "ac75d914-2ab5-597e-880b-b113374d3b98" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322618 1145 "To determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(-1),$ we use the following formula:\n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(-1)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(-1))}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the value of ${f}^{-1}(-1).$ To do this, we solve the equation ${f}^{-1}(-1)=x.$ For $x\\ne 2,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-1}(-1) & =x \\\\ f(x) & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{x}{x-2} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{x}{x-2}\\cdot (x-2) & =-1\\cdot (x-2) \\\\ \\frac{x}{\\cancel{(x-2)}}\\cdot \\cancel{(x-2)} & =-x+2 \\\\ x & =-x+2 \\\\ 2x & =2 \\\\ x & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{-1}(-1)=1.$\n\nNow we calculate ${f}^{′}(1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x}{x-2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{′}(1) & =-\\frac{2}{{(1-2)}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(-1) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(-1))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-2)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322619 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322620 13194139534958 true] [17592186322619 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322621 13194139534958 true] [17592186322619 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534958 true] [17592186322619 1041 "field-1" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322619 1104 #edb/ref 17592186322620 13194139534958 true] [17592186322619 1110 #uuid "86de29c8-fd36-5055-a676-eb157138c37a" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322620 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322620 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534958 true] [17592186322620 1111 #uuid "35e953fa-2550-58b9-9743-9afaef438fa8" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322621 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534958 true] [17592186322621 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534958 true] [17592186322621 1111 #uuid "35f358df-5b62-5ee3-818a-93cb85af9888" 13194139534958 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-312579" 17592186322611 "q-312579/field-1" 17592186322612 "q-312579/field-1/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e